WEBVTT

01:42.018 --> 01:46.940
WHAT LIES AT THE END OF THE MELON PATCH

01:59.702 --> 02:01.913
MEAT EATERS FEST

02:02.580 --> 02:03.623
<i>What's going on?</i>

02:04.582 --> 02:06.584
OPENING SALE

02:06.668 --> 02:09.170
<i>Looks like everyone's enjoying themselves.</i>

02:10.547 --> 02:12.006
CONGRATULATIONS!
OPENING SALE

02:15.468 --> 02:16.469
Hello!

02:16.553 --> 02:19.305
Me? I didn't order any udon.

02:19.806 --> 02:23.393
No, I wanted to ask...
Is there some kind of festival today?

02:23.935 --> 02:26.980
You haven't heard?
I thought all the carnivores knew by now.

02:27.063 --> 02:28.565
Yeah.

02:28.648 --> 02:30.150
Take a look.

02:31.401 --> 02:32.527
YAHYA IS DEAD!

02:32.610 --> 02:33.611
Mr. Yahya?

02:33.695 --> 02:34.696
What?

02:34.779 --> 02:38.074
I've never heard anyone
call him "Mr." before.

02:40.326 --> 02:44.914
With Yahya gone, we can sell
all the meat we want! Time to celebrate!

02:44.998 --> 02:48.585
The customers don't have to
worry about being caught either.

02:49.127 --> 02:52.046
So Mr. Yahya is really dead?

02:52.672 --> 02:54.090
I wonder.

02:54.173 --> 02:55.884
It could be a trick, I suppose.

02:55.967 --> 02:58.261
I doubt Yahya could be killed so easily.

02:58.344 --> 03:00.972
Yeah. He's so strong.

03:01.055 --> 03:04.601
You mean you've fought him before?

03:04.684 --> 03:07.937
What? Well, I...

03:08.021 --> 03:12.150
Wow! So that scar
on your face is the real deal!

03:12.233 --> 03:17.280
People were saying that he'd lost
some of his strength with age.

03:17.363 --> 03:20.033
I suppose it is possible
that someone finally got him.

03:20.950 --> 03:24.245
<i>I don't necessarily like
Mr. Yahya's policies either,</i>

03:24.787 --> 03:28.917
<i>so I can't blame the carnivores
for celebrating.</i>

03:29.000 --> 03:31.294
Young man,
don't you have a delivery to make?

03:31.794 --> 03:34.797
That's right! Bye!

03:59.781 --> 04:02.992
These are being distributed
around the Black Market.

04:03.701 --> 04:06.079
We believe it's
the work of that counselor.

04:06.162 --> 04:08.122
We've been trying
to track his location, but...

04:09.332 --> 04:11.251
we haven't made much progress.

04:11.334 --> 04:15.630
<i>He knows perfectly well I'm alive.</i>

04:16.339 --> 04:17.715
<i>What is he planning?</i>

04:18.508 --> 04:22.428
We'd be screwed
if he was hiding in the Black Market,

04:22.512 --> 04:25.056
but him being an herbivore,
I doubt that's the case.

04:25.139 --> 04:29.060
<i>My name is Melon. Don't forget it.</i>

04:29.727 --> 04:33.064
Corne. Expand our search
into the Black Market.

04:33.147 --> 04:34.857
What? But...

04:34.941 --> 04:40.863
This Melon may have the face of one,
but he's no normal gazelle.

04:41.489 --> 04:43.866
He has the fangs of a carnivore.

04:43.950 --> 04:44.784
What?

04:44.867 --> 04:46.786
He's a mix.

04:47.287 --> 04:48.288
A mix?

04:48.913 --> 04:51.499
That means he has a hunter's instincts.

04:51.582 --> 04:53.459
Damn. I've been fooled!

04:53.960 --> 04:56.754
I'll expand the search area at once.

04:56.838 --> 04:58.172
Hoo boy, he got us good.

04:58.840 --> 05:01.009
He's a mix, of course...

05:01.884 --> 05:04.137
<i>Why did he show me his face?</i>

05:05.138 --> 05:08.349
<i>Just when we were
getting to know each other.</i>

05:08.891 --> 05:11.936
<i>Sorry you won't make it to the party.</i>

05:12.937 --> 05:15.315
<i>Was that a challenge?</i>

05:17.608 --> 05:22.322
<i>An invitation for the only one
who knows your face?</i>

05:24.032 --> 05:26.409
<i>Or was it blackmail?</i>

05:28.036 --> 05:29.037
<i>Melon.</i>

05:30.204 --> 05:31.748
<i>I will capture you...</i>

05:32.498 --> 05:35.752
<i>and turn you into fertilizer
for my sweet, little carrots.</i>

05:39.505 --> 05:43.342
UDON BEBEBE

05:43.926 --> 05:48.765
<i>After the Madara-Gumi drug production ring
was exposed by the Beastars last year...</i>

05:48.848 --> 05:51.267
<i>The Black Market was in an uproar...</i>

05:51.893 --> 05:55.730
<i>but the news hasn't mentioned
Mr. Yahya once.</i>

05:57.106 --> 06:00.485
<i>Maybe it's not for me to worry about.</i>

06:00.568 --> 06:02.028
<i>In other news,</i>

06:03.071 --> 06:05.948
<i>the Committee for Coexistence
and Mutual Prosperity</i>

06:06.032 --> 06:12.914
<i>will offer financial aid to families
with mixed children from this month.</i>

06:13.956 --> 06:16.918
<i>Called the Live Together Support Fund,</i>

06:17.001 --> 06:21.798
<i>it has been designed to support
families in interspecies marriages,</i>

06:21.881 --> 06:26.302
<i>who still face discrimination
despite being recognized by law.</i>

06:26.844 --> 06:29.972
<i>I didn't know they did this kind of thing.</i>

06:30.598 --> 06:31.682
Give me a break.

06:32.600 --> 06:36.604
Why are they using our tax money
for crap like this?

06:36.687 --> 06:39.816
They give it a fancy name
like "interspecies relationships,"

06:39.899 --> 06:44.403
but in reality it's just a bunch of
irresponsible youngsters having kids.

06:44.987 --> 06:47.490
Call it discrimination,
but that's what you get.

06:47.573 --> 06:48.449
Right?

06:51.119 --> 06:52.411
- More noodles.
- Right.

06:54.789 --> 06:56.040
One refill.

06:56.541 --> 06:57.542
Coming up.

06:58.584 --> 07:00.795
Don't let him get to you.

07:00.878 --> 07:03.047
All sorts of animals come to eat here.

07:03.714 --> 07:05.550
Oh, I'm fine.

07:06.425 --> 07:08.761
You're getting good at working the hall.

07:09.262 --> 07:10.263
Really?

07:10.346 --> 07:14.225
At first, you were afraid
to even go near our herbivore customers.

07:14.308 --> 07:16.144
I wasn't sure you could do it.

07:16.644 --> 07:18.438
Well, I...

07:19.856 --> 07:20.857
I get it.

07:21.399 --> 07:23.359
I'm a carnivore too.

07:23.443 --> 07:26.737
When I first opened up,
not a single herbivore came to eat here.

07:27.321 --> 07:31.742
Really? What made them start coming?

07:33.327 --> 07:35.746
It was the udon, of course.

07:36.414 --> 07:39.208
The herbivores
who started out only getting delivery

07:39.292 --> 07:41.502
wanted to try the noodles
fresh out of the pot.

07:42.128 --> 07:43.963
That's the power of delicious food.

07:45.423 --> 07:48.843
Instead of talking about
this "live together" stuff,

07:49.510 --> 07:54.432
if we can enjoy eating good food together,
everyone will be happy.

07:55.600 --> 07:58.019
You know, you might be right.

07:58.936 --> 08:00.730
Well, don't just stand there.

08:01.564 --> 08:03.441
Our customer's waiting.

08:04.192 --> 08:05.026
Right!

08:23.669 --> 08:24.670
Back then,

08:25.713 --> 08:27.924
we had a wood table in the kitchen, right?

08:28.883 --> 08:30.051
Do you remember, Mom?

08:31.177 --> 08:38.142
I loved gathering around that table
and eating with you and Grandpa.

08:39.352 --> 08:43.523
I always thought how nice
it'd be to have a family of my own.

08:45.191 --> 08:47.735
I'm seeing this girl, you know.

08:47.818 --> 08:51.280
She's actually a dwarf rabbit.

08:51.405 --> 08:53.074
A dwarf rabbit?

08:53.991 --> 08:54.992
Grandpa?

08:55.952 --> 08:59.205
Sorry, I wasn't trying to eavesdrop.

08:59.789 --> 09:04.001
But was that true? You're dating a rabbit?

09:04.502 --> 09:05.336
Yeah.

09:06.003 --> 09:08.798
I want to marry her one day.

09:08.881 --> 09:10.091
Are you serious?

09:10.591 --> 09:15.680
You should know how hard it is
to be an interspecies family.

09:15.763 --> 09:19.559
- And between an herbivore and a carnivore...
- I'm ready for it.

09:20.726 --> 09:21.894
I'm serious about this.

09:22.436 --> 09:24.897
I've thought about it a lot.
I've trained for it.

09:25.731 --> 09:29.569
I told you before. I'm not a kid anymore.

09:31.487 --> 09:32.321
I see.

09:33.155 --> 09:37.076
You're right.
You've become a fine young man.

09:39.287 --> 09:45.501
I wasn't able to deal with the pain
your mother went through as a mix.

09:46.043 --> 09:47.044
Why not?

09:48.170 --> 09:53.175
I think I was always too scared
to broach the subject.

09:53.259 --> 09:56.220
But you and I are not the same.

09:56.846 --> 10:00.141
You're the kind of guy
who gives people flowers.

10:01.726 --> 10:03.144
You'll do just fine.

10:04.895 --> 10:06.606
Thank you, Grandpa.

10:09.191 --> 10:12.278
- You punk.
- Ow! Cut it out!

10:16.866 --> 10:19.160
So, you'd like to sell your shell?

10:20.703 --> 10:24.540
As part of our Yahya's Dead Campaign,
I'll operate without anesthesia!

10:25.041 --> 10:27.960
Wait! What kind of campaign is that?

10:28.044 --> 10:31.088
Shells shrink up due to fear,
concentrating their benefits,

10:31.172 --> 10:33.841
so I'll buy it at a higher price!

10:33.924 --> 10:35.509
That's the campaign!

10:35.593 --> 10:38.596
I don't care about the price,
just give me anesthesia!

10:41.807 --> 10:44.727
Hey! You can't just come in here!

10:50.316 --> 10:52.276
Yahya?

10:52.360 --> 10:53.986
You're alive?

10:54.070 --> 10:54.904
Yes.

10:55.946 --> 10:57.907
Guess that's the end of your campaign.

11:00.701 --> 11:02.703
What can I do for you?

11:02.787 --> 11:05.665
I'm in the middle of
a legitimate medical procedure, so--

11:05.748 --> 11:09.543
Enough small talk. I don't have time.

11:10.086 --> 11:16.967
I want to know where you got
elephant ivory to make the Hyperdrug.

11:17.051 --> 11:18.761
That's a trade secret.

11:23.224 --> 11:24.892
I'm not a patient man.

11:25.476 --> 11:26.477
Stop!

11:27.144 --> 11:29.146
Answer me.

11:29.772 --> 11:32.900
Unless you want me to squash you first.

11:33.484 --> 11:34.985
It was the gazelle! The gazelle!

11:35.069 --> 11:38.531
A crazy herbivore just brought it to us!

11:38.614 --> 11:39.824
You sure about that?

11:39.907 --> 11:42.034
I couldn't see his face behind his mask,

11:42.118 --> 11:43.953
but those horns are unmistakable.

11:44.036 --> 11:47.289
So you took the goods
from this mysterious gazelle?

11:47.373 --> 11:51.502
Yes. Normally it's the Shishi-Gumi
who supplies it,

11:51.585 --> 11:56.507
but he used ivory to bribe them
into making him their boss.

11:57.133 --> 12:00.970
Please don't tell anyone
you heard this from me!

12:02.388 --> 12:04.974
I'll keep my mouth shut!
Just give me anesthesia!

12:09.812 --> 12:12.356
Here. The report, as requested.

12:13.065 --> 12:14.024
I appreciate it.

12:14.984 --> 12:16.068
You better.

12:16.152 --> 12:18.904
Unlike you students, I'm actually busy.

12:19.405 --> 12:20.698
Anything of interest?

12:25.494 --> 12:28.581
It's mostly a normal energy drink,

12:29.206 --> 12:31.500
but there are some
strange things mixed in.

12:31.584 --> 12:32.585
Strange?

12:32.668 --> 12:35.296
Components that would
normally go undetected.

12:35.379 --> 12:37.631
I wonder how they got there?

12:38.424 --> 12:39.842
I look forward to seeing it.

12:40.634 --> 12:45.139
I don't know what you're up to,
but let me know if you find anything fun.

12:45.931 --> 12:50.019
We'll see. It may be something
you're better off not knowing.

13:01.238 --> 13:04.575
Hey, wake up. Time for your shift.

13:10.623 --> 13:12.291
How's it going inside?

13:12.374 --> 13:16.253
Quiet as a mouse.
They're just playing cards and drinking.

13:16.921 --> 13:18.881
Guess Melon's not coming back.

13:26.430 --> 13:27.348
Hey, Norris!

13:29.683 --> 13:32.770
Hey, I don't wanna die. Eyes on the road.

13:32.853 --> 13:34.688
Didn't you hear that just now?

13:34.772 --> 13:35.898
Hear what?

13:35.981 --> 13:37.983
Forget it.

13:57.002 --> 14:00.839
Can't we do this
at a more reasonable hour?

14:00.923 --> 14:03.759
I called you as soon as it was ready.

14:03.842 --> 14:06.178
What do you think? Beautiful, isn't it?

14:06.262 --> 14:11.225
It took a lot of work
to make this much deer shit.

14:11.308 --> 14:14.770
You sure have a thing for shit.

14:14.853 --> 14:17.565
No, it's the public that loves mine!

14:20.067 --> 14:22.194
Wait, this is all you got?

14:22.278 --> 14:24.321
Yes. That's all of it.

14:24.405 --> 14:26.574
That's not nearly enough.

14:26.657 --> 14:29.952
It's not as easily produced
as that shoddy Kines stuff.

14:30.452 --> 14:33.414
There's only so much
that can be made in one batch.

14:33.497 --> 14:35.541
This isn't what we talked about!

14:35.624 --> 14:37.960
Getting angry won't change anything.

14:38.043 --> 14:39.670
It's difficult to synthesize.

14:40.254 --> 14:43.257
But I have confidence in each drop.

14:43.340 --> 14:44.341
But...

14:44.425 --> 14:47.720
Besides, the rarer it is,
the higher the demand, right?

14:47.803 --> 14:51.348
This will make you and your boss
famous overnight.

14:52.391 --> 14:54.143
Now, please sign here.

14:56.562 --> 14:59.023
I'm handing over my finest batch.

14:59.982 --> 15:03.444
It will please carnivores
and herbivores alike.

15:03.527 --> 15:05.988
It will be loved by all.

15:06.071 --> 15:08.073
- Just like me.
- Shut up!

15:08.699 --> 15:11.035
Give us the full amount next time!

15:11.619 --> 15:14.663
Then I'll need your help
gathering droppings again.

15:14.747 --> 15:15.998
You wish!

15:32.097 --> 15:34.058
What now?

15:34.600 --> 15:37.311
Doesn't it smell like sewage to you?

15:37.394 --> 15:39.355
That's just your mane.

15:39.438 --> 15:40.439
Cut it out.

15:41.523 --> 15:43.442
Am I imagining things?

15:43.525 --> 15:45.152
Hey, look out!

15:48.197 --> 15:50.699
What did I tell you? Eyes on the road!

15:50.783 --> 15:52.743
I'm sorry! I'll be careful!

15:52.826 --> 15:55.955
- You guys, I swear!
- It won't happen again.

15:56.038 --> 15:57.998
- Forward! Look forward!
- Yes, sir!

16:04.046 --> 16:05.297
<i>What is this?</i>

16:10.469 --> 16:12.221
Where should we put it?

16:12.304 --> 16:14.348
Just leave it on the counter.

16:14.473 --> 16:15.307
Got it.

16:20.145 --> 16:21.522
You know,

16:21.605 --> 16:24.942
we've put so much work into this.

16:25.025 --> 16:27.528
Do you think we'll get to try the stuff?

16:27.611 --> 16:29.405
Doubt it.

16:29.488 --> 16:31.115
Seems to be pretty damn important.

16:31.198 --> 16:32.199
Yeah.

16:32.282 --> 16:36.870
Enough to make the boss want to
reveal it himself at the masquerade.

16:37.371 --> 16:40.833
It's unlike him, isn't it?
He usually doesn't show his face.

16:41.417 --> 16:43.836
All right. That oughta do it.

16:43.919 --> 16:45.838
That's fine.

16:49.008 --> 16:52.970
I won't be getting much sleep tonight.
And we have more prep in the morning.

16:53.846 --> 16:54.847
I'm beat.

16:57.766 --> 16:59.935
I knew I heard something!

17:00.019 --> 17:01.854
I know you're in here.

17:03.480 --> 17:04.565
Huh?

17:04.690 --> 17:06.942
I told you nothing's there.

17:07.484 --> 17:10.029
You're such a scaredy cat.

17:10.112 --> 17:13.240
Why don't you try being more lion-like?

17:15.200 --> 17:17.578
I'm not feeling great today.

17:17.661 --> 17:19.872
- Will you take over the driving?
- Hell no.

17:19.955 --> 17:20.789
Dang.

17:34.261 --> 17:35.763
INVITATION
MASQUERADE PARTY

17:35.846 --> 17:40.267
<i>Looks like the Shishi-Gumi
is hosting a masquerade party.</i>

17:41.685 --> 17:43.228
I see.

17:44.021 --> 17:46.356
So that's the party he mentioned.

17:47.691 --> 17:49.485
Sounds fun, doesn't it?

17:49.568 --> 17:51.695
I'll arrange support right away.

17:51.779 --> 17:55.532
No, this is between me and him.

17:55.616 --> 17:58.368
Don't tell me you plan on going alone?

17:59.787 --> 18:02.039
I didn't say that.

18:26.188 --> 18:29.399
Mr. Yahya! So you <i>are</i> alive!

18:30.067 --> 18:32.402
Were you worried about me?

18:33.278 --> 18:36.949
I'm surprised you got through
the fifth-floor window on that leg.

18:37.032 --> 18:40.202
I didn't use my legs, I used this.

18:42.079 --> 18:44.414
So... what do you want?

18:44.498 --> 18:47.918
Wait, didn't you pull your fangs out?

18:48.001 --> 18:51.505
Oh, these? They're dentures.

18:51.588 --> 18:53.423
I need them to talk.

18:53.507 --> 18:56.218
To talk, huh? That's just like you.

18:57.010 --> 18:59.054
Here's a souvenir.

19:01.557 --> 19:02.641
A melon?

19:02.724 --> 19:07.646
Legoshi. Are melons vegetables or fruits?

19:10.274 --> 19:12.442
They're fruits, aren't they?

19:12.526 --> 19:14.820
Fruits grow on trees.

19:14.903 --> 19:16.488
Oh, that's right.

19:16.572 --> 19:18.407
So, it's a vegetable?

19:18.490 --> 19:20.659
Do you eat vegetables for dessert?

19:21.160 --> 19:23.328
No, I guess not. Which is it?

19:24.705 --> 19:27.374
Maybe it's a fruit-like vegetable?

19:29.126 --> 19:31.378
That's a nice compromise.

19:31.461 --> 19:33.797
Who cares, anyway?

19:34.882 --> 19:38.385
I don't like things
that aren't black and white.

19:38.886 --> 19:45.726
Like a carnivore removing his own fangs
and claiming to be equal to herbivores.

19:46.268 --> 19:48.187
Are you here to get me back for that?

19:48.270 --> 19:52.274
Or children born
from a carnivore and an herbivore.

19:54.443 --> 19:59.823
The criminal I'm after
is a carnivore-herbivore mix.

19:59.907 --> 20:00.908
A mix?

20:01.617 --> 20:04.369
His name is Melon.

20:05.454 --> 20:06.580
What did he do?

20:07.247 --> 20:10.959
He disguises himself as an herbivore
to get close to them.

20:11.043 --> 20:13.795
Then, as soon as they
let their guard down, he strikes.

20:14.838 --> 20:16.506
He sounds like a nasty devourer.

20:16.590 --> 20:19.301
No, he hasn't devoured anyone.

20:20.302 --> 20:22.721
He kills them, but doesn't eat them.

20:23.222 --> 20:25.182
He simply enjoys the act of killing.

20:26.391 --> 20:29.519
That's even worse than devouring,
don't you think?

20:30.437 --> 20:31.730
But why?

20:32.231 --> 20:35.651
I'll have to ask him.

20:35.734 --> 20:38.737
So why are you here talking to me?

20:38.820 --> 20:40.239
You need to go catch him.

20:40.322 --> 20:46.161
I'd love to, but for a horse,
a leg wound is fatal.

20:46.245 --> 20:47.371
I see.

20:48.413 --> 20:53.377
Will you help me in the capture
of the savage mix Melon?

20:55.754 --> 20:59.466
I know. It's a highly dangerous mission.

20:59.549 --> 21:02.552
It wouldn't be for free.
How about ten million?

21:03.303 --> 21:04.680
What?

21:05.180 --> 21:08.392
What are you talking about?
I don't need your money.

21:08.475 --> 21:11.853
I'm living the way I want
with my udon shop gig.

21:12.437 --> 21:16.358
And are you planning
to start a humble family

21:16.441 --> 21:18.986
with that cute rabbit friend of yours?

21:19.069 --> 21:20.570
Leave me alone.

21:20.654 --> 21:22.072
Why me?

21:22.155 --> 21:25.367
Is it because I'm the grandson
of your old partner, Gosha?

21:27.327 --> 21:28.662
No.

21:28.745 --> 21:32.749
I just thought I'd give you
a peek into your future.

21:34.710 --> 21:38.588
What do you get when you cross
a carnivore with an herbivore?

21:38.672 --> 21:42.092
What kind of twisted creature
would be born?

21:43.885 --> 21:47.097
<i>Haru and my... child?</i>

22:00.485 --> 22:01.653
Legoshi!

23:36.915 --> 23:41.920
Subtitle translation by: Thomas Grathwol
